<title>GERMANY: Jagoda sees average 4.3 mln German jobless in 1997.</title>
<headline>Jagoda sees average 4.3 mln German jobless in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Federal Labour Office president Bernhard Jagoda said that staying within the 4.3 million average jobless corridor was still a possibility in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;If the September figures do not show an improvement, I will have to reexamine my forecast,&quot; he told a news conference after releasing jobless figures for July.</p>
<p>Jagoda added that reducing average unemployment in 1998 to around &quot;four million&quot; is possible.</p>
</text>
